WEBVTT

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:43.385
They said
it couldn't be done, Kif.

00:00:43.468 --> 00:00:45.637
But here we are,
stealing an unlimited supply

00:00:45.721 --> 00:00:49.182
of birthday-grade helium
from the unsuspecting moon.

00:00:49.266 --> 00:00:50.517
Sun.

00:00:50.601 --> 00:00:52.185
At night,
it's called the moon.

00:00:52.269 --> 00:00:55.772
All this heat
has rendered me parch-ed.

00:00:55.856 --> 00:00:58.275
Which of this doo-whackies
dispenses Horchata?

00:00:59.568 --> 00:01:01.904
Stop! That's the force field
holding the mine open!

00:01:07.242 --> 00:01:09.703
Mine collapse!
Mine collapse!

00:01:09.786 --> 00:01:11.747
So? Mine collapse, too.

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:20.339
15 miners are now confirmed
trapped in the sun.

00:01:20.422 --> 00:01:22.215
If rescue doesn't come soon,

00:01:22.299 --> 00:01:25.219
they may never again
not see the light of day.

00:01:25.302 --> 00:01:28.055
Linda?

00:01:28.138 --> 00:01:29.890
The situation is grim, Morbo.

00:01:29.973 --> 00:01:32.351
Officials concede that
any attempt at rescue

00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:34.394
would be an agonizing
suicide mission.

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:37.522
Good news, everyone!

00:01:38.857 --> 00:01:40.567
When the mine caved in,

00:01:40.651 --> 00:01:43.237
the entrance was blocked
by a fusion explosion.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:46.073
Luckily, the miners
found safe haven here

00:01:46.156 --> 00:01:48.700
in the doom chamber.

00:01:48.784 --> 00:01:51.703
To rescue them, you'll simply
have to fly to the sun

00:01:51.787 --> 00:01:55.582
and march in through
an inferno of molten plasma.

00:01:55.666 --> 00:01:58.710
But solar plasma is,
like, 10,000 degrees hot.

00:01:58.794 --> 00:02:00.545
Won't that sear
our tender flesh,

00:02:00.629 --> 00:02:02.047
sealing in the juices?

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:03.590
Oh, nonsense.

00:02:03.674 --> 00:02:06.802
You clearly weren't paying attention
to what I'm about to say.

00:02:06.885 --> 00:02:08.762
To the sub-basement!

00:02:12.307 --> 00:02:15.060
You see, you'll be protected
by my fermion barrier

00:02:15.143 --> 00:02:16.436
heat-exclusion spray.

00:02:17.854 --> 00:02:20.148
Watch as I demonstrate
by coating

00:02:20.232 --> 00:02:22.651
some highly delicate matter,
and dunking it

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:25.279
into this molten lava.

00:02:33.954 --> 00:02:35.914
Guess what.
Hell is real.

00:02:36.164 --> 00:02:37.958
Oh, good, it works.

00:02:38.041 --> 00:02:40.085
Toodle-oo!

00:02:56.435 --> 00:02:57.728
Prepare for action.

00:02:57.811 --> 00:02:58.979
Aye-aye.

00:03:10.365 --> 00:03:12.576
Attention, helium miners.

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:14.202
Can you hear me?

00:03:14.286 --> 00:03:16.038
For God's sake, help us!

00:03:16.121 --> 00:03:18.540
We're in agonizing pain!

00:03:20.334 --> 00:03:21.627
Stop laughing.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:24.087
Help is on the way!

00:03:24.379 --> 00:03:28.008
In the meantime, you should sing a song
to keep your spirits up.

00:03:28.091 --> 00:03:30.302
How about "Camptown Races"?

00:03:30.385 --> 00:03:32.596
Camptown ladies, sing this song

00:03:32.679 --> 00:03:34.973
Doo dah, doo dah...

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:39.144
Let's do this.

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:45.776
I'll stay here and be
in charge of not dying.

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:55.410
Razzma flazzma plasma.

00:03:55.494 --> 00:03:57.829
We must be close,
we're hitting an occasional...

00:03:57.913 --> 00:03:58.914
...helium pocket.

00:04:02.376 --> 00:04:03.877
We don't have much time!

00:04:03.961 --> 00:04:05.170
Keep moving forward!

00:04:05.254 --> 00:04:07.464
Screw that! I'm getting out of here.

00:04:12.427 --> 00:04:15.847
Just one more fire between me
and a well-earned nap.

00:04:18.225 --> 00:04:20.852
Whoa!

00:04:20.936 --> 00:04:23.480
What a dramatic scene, Linda.

00:04:23.564 --> 00:04:26.942
The heroic robot,
withno concern for his own safety,

00:04:27.025 --> 00:04:29.820
has bravely charged
back into the mine.

00:04:29.903 --> 00:04:30.904
What else is on?

00:04:44.876 --> 00:04:47.754
P.U.! It is ripe in here.

00:04:47.838 --> 00:04:49.798
Well, so long, jerks.

00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:55.721
We're now in minute five of
our round-the-clock coverage

00:04:55.804 --> 00:04:58.807
as we await the return
of the courageous robot.

00:05:02.269 --> 00:05:03.645
Ooh.

00:05:03.729 --> 00:05:05.480
What the...?

00:05:05.564 --> 00:05:06.815
How'd that get in there?

00:05:06.899 --> 00:05:09.443
Thank you.
Thank you, sir.

00:05:09.526 --> 00:05:10.903
You're a true hero.

00:05:10.986 --> 00:05:11.987
I am?

00:05:12.112 --> 00:05:15.198
Huh, I always strongly suspected
I was one of those.

00:05:15.282 --> 00:05:16.992
One man is safe.

00:05:17.075 --> 00:05:20.412
But who will the robot pull next
from the fiery hole of mystery?

00:05:20.495 --> 00:05:23.081
An actress?
A celebrity chef?

00:05:23.165 --> 00:05:26.293
Stay tuned for the next 14 rescues.

00:05:26.376 --> 00:05:28.629
14?

00:05:49.316 --> 00:05:50.651
And that's the final miner!

00:05:50.734 --> 00:05:52.194
They all made it!

00:05:53.362 --> 00:05:54.696
Morbo is not weeping.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:57.741
He has a, a parasite in his eye.

00:05:59.534 --> 00:06:02.120
Whoo! I'm the greatest!

00:06:07.626 --> 00:06:09.211
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:06:09.294 --> 00:06:12.297
we're here today
to pay tribute to the heroic

00:06:12.381 --> 00:06:13.882
Planet Express crew!

00:06:13.966 --> 00:06:15.968
But we only have the one medal.

00:06:16.051 --> 00:06:18.595
So please direct all your
admiration to the main guy...

00:06:18.679 --> 00:06:19.930
Bender!

00:06:21.682 --> 00:06:23.308
Now, you two step aside.

00:06:27.771 --> 00:06:30.148
Hey, being a hero's all right.

00:06:30.232 --> 00:06:31.775
Look at all this free stuff.

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:33.735
Oh, my God, you guys, fire!

00:06:33.819 --> 00:06:35.112
Fire!

00:06:38.574 --> 00:06:40.701
My baby's in that podium!

00:06:40.784 --> 00:06:42.619
Somebody call
the fire department!

00:06:42.703 --> 00:06:44.371
There is no fire department.

00:06:44.454 --> 00:06:46.206
I sold it to pay
for Bender's medal.

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:47.708
Hold this, your highness.

00:06:47.791 --> 00:06:49.501
You'll need to award it
to me again in a minute.

00:07:00.721 --> 00:07:03.557
These boys must have
hero in their bones.

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:06.727
And you, ma'am, must have
heroine in your veins.

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:08.270
I hereby decree

00:07:08.353 --> 00:07:12.524
Planet Express to be
our city's new fire department!

00:07:12.608 --> 00:07:14.526
Bite my shiny metal axe!

00:07:17.654 --> 00:07:20.282
And you, give me back my medal.

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:37.549
Friends, look at
these new poles.

00:07:37.633 --> 00:07:40.719
Get ready
for one sexy firehouse.

00:07:40.802 --> 00:07:44.431
Zoidberg, quit turning us on
and go polish your nozzle.

00:07:44.514 --> 00:07:46.516
Yo! Hero in the house.

00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:49.394
I just got back
from my daily medal strut.

00:07:51.521 --> 00:07:53.690
What's that?
Did they pick a new Pope?

00:07:53.774 --> 00:07:55.692
Good news, everyone!

00:07:55.776 --> 00:07:57.611
Someone's home is on fire.

00:08:51.623 --> 00:08:52.958
I'm exhausted.

00:08:53.041 --> 00:08:56.003
All this firefighting
is murder on my feet.

00:08:57.921 --> 00:09:00.090
There has been quite
a rash of fires lately.

00:09:00.173 --> 00:09:02.634
First at the podium
where Bender got his medal.

00:09:02.718 --> 00:09:05.846
Then that house next door to
Bender's favorite strip club.

00:09:05.929 --> 00:09:07.764
Robot Hell had a fire, too.

00:09:07.848 --> 00:09:10.267
Right after Bender was there
for a workshop.

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:12.185
And don't forget
that vampire bank

00:09:12.269 --> 00:09:15.522
where the robot keeps his hero
medals in a safe deposit box.

00:09:15.606 --> 00:09:18.525
Hmm. I think I'm
noticing a pattern.

00:09:18.609 --> 00:09:19.943
My God, you're right!

00:09:20.027 --> 00:09:22.863
The locations form
a perfect shape of some kind.

00:09:22.946 --> 00:09:25.198
No! Bender was at every one

00:09:25.282 --> 00:09:27.910
of those places
right before the fire started.

00:09:27.993 --> 00:09:30.579
Sweet pyro of Cairo! That's true!

00:09:30.662 --> 00:09:33.874
Could Bender be setting these
fires just so he can be a hero?

00:09:33.957 --> 00:09:35.459
- Oh, I don't know.
- Possible, feasible.

00:09:35.542 --> 00:09:36.835
- Seems like maybe.
- Who knows?

00:09:36.919 --> 00:09:38.253
Yeah, probably.

00:09:38.337 --> 00:09:41.006
How dare you murmur
about Bender like that!

00:09:41.089 --> 00:09:43.634
He would never burn something
down to get attention.

00:09:43.717 --> 00:09:45.052
For insurance money? Yes.

00:09:45.135 --> 00:09:46.720
Revenge? You bet.

00:09:46.803 --> 00:09:49.431
To give an autumn night
that crisp chestnutty smell?

00:09:49.514 --> 00:09:50.515
Absolutely.

00:09:50.599 --> 00:09:53.477
But not for fame,
women or thrills.

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:55.437
Hey, guys, it's me, Bender.

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:57.105
The famous, sexy, thrilling hero.

00:09:58.774 --> 00:10:00.359
So now that we're a firehouse,

00:10:00.442 --> 00:10:02.069
we should make
some firehouse chili.

00:10:02.152 --> 00:10:04.613
What do you want in that,
beans or just blood?

00:10:06.782 --> 00:10:09.785
Oh, no! Surprisingly,
a fire has broken out

00:10:09.868 --> 00:10:11.370
at the meat market where I am!

00:10:11.453 --> 00:10:13.705
We'll be there right away.

00:10:13.789 --> 00:10:15.290
Yeah, don't trouble yourselves.

00:10:15.374 --> 00:10:17.125
This is just a one-hero fire.

00:10:29.471 --> 00:10:30.472
- Mr. Bender!
- Over here, over here!

00:10:30.556 --> 00:10:31.974
Small quote from
you, Mr. Bender.

00:10:32.057 --> 00:10:34.142
Scoop Chang,
"New New York Magazine,"

00:10:34.226 --> 00:10:35.727
Kosher Recipes Editor,
iPad Edition.

00:10:35.811 --> 00:10:37.437
Ma'am, what
happened in there?

00:10:37.521 --> 00:10:39.690
Well, I was shoplifting
a lamb chop

00:10:39.773 --> 00:10:42.859
when suddenly fire erupted
from the liver tray.

00:10:42.943 --> 00:10:44.778
Next thing I knew,
I was carried to safety

00:10:44.861 --> 00:10:47.281
by this strapping
young whatchacallit.

00:10:47.364 --> 00:10:48.365
Hero.

00:10:48.448 --> 00:10:50.826
- Hero.
- Aw, stop.

00:10:50.909 --> 00:10:52.077
Keep going.

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:00.210
We know what you've
been doing, Bender.

00:11:00.294 --> 00:11:01.795
You've been setting
all those fires

00:11:01.878 --> 00:11:03.463
because you're addicted
to glory.

00:11:03.547 --> 00:11:05.674
What? The very idea!

00:11:05.757 --> 00:11:07.467
Don't try to deny it!

00:11:07.551 --> 00:11:08.886
You're out of the squad!

00:11:08.969 --> 00:11:10.262
Out of the squad?

00:11:10.345 --> 00:11:11.722
I am the squad!

00:11:11.805 --> 00:11:13.390
You believe me, don't you, Fry?

00:11:13.473 --> 00:11:15.058
I don't know, Bender.

00:11:15.142 --> 00:11:17.644
You got to admit, the pattern of fires
is suspicious,

00:11:17.728 --> 00:11:19.521
being a perfect shape and all.

00:11:19.605 --> 00:11:22.399
We can't have
an arsonist in our midst.

00:11:22.482 --> 00:11:26.361
We can have four idiots and
a fat guy, but no arsonists.

00:11:26.445 --> 00:11:28.947
Now clean out your
locker and beat it!

00:11:32.826 --> 00:11:36.246
They can't do this to me,
Bender, a well-known hero.

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:37.998
I'm the world's
greatest firefighter!

00:11:39.207 --> 00:11:40.584
Fire!

00:11:47.966 --> 00:11:48.967
What the...

00:11:49.051 --> 00:11:52.012
What kind of crazy fire is this?

00:11:53.472 --> 00:11:55.891
Greetings, Bender.

00:11:55.974 --> 00:11:57.809
Thank you for transporting me

00:11:57.893 --> 00:12:01.396
from the sun to your helpless,
flammable planet.

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:03.232
How could a fire learn to talk?

00:12:03.315 --> 00:12:04.733
Did you burn up a dictionary?

00:12:04.816 --> 00:12:06.318
Or a parrot?

00:12:06.401 --> 00:12:09.488
I am a being of pure solar energy.

00:12:09.571 --> 00:12:12.032
My race inhabits the nuclear inferno

00:12:12.115 --> 00:12:14.451
of the sun's photosphere.

00:12:14.534 --> 00:12:16.370
You're a chatty little fire, aren't ya?

00:12:16.453 --> 00:12:20.165
A billion years ago,
I attempted to overthrow

00:12:20.249 --> 00:12:24.044
the democratically elected
alderman from my district.

00:12:24.127 --> 00:12:26.421
But I was captured and imprisoned.

00:12:26.505 --> 00:12:27.923
Fools!

00:12:28.006 --> 00:12:31.969
Then you arrived and provided me
a means of escape.

00:12:32.052 --> 00:12:34.888
Get to the point,
Flame-O.

00:12:34.972 --> 00:12:36.848
If I can't rule the sun,

00:12:36.932 --> 00:12:40.561
I shall ignite your planet
and rule here instead.

00:12:42.187 --> 00:12:43.855
So you set all those fires.

00:12:43.939 --> 00:12:45.399
You framed me!

00:12:45.482 --> 00:12:48.277
You're huffin' for a snuffin', boy!

00:12:50.779 --> 00:12:52.030
Foolish robot.

00:12:52.114 --> 00:12:55.117
No power on Earth
can extinguish me!

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:56.743
Oh, yeah?

00:12:56.827 --> 00:13:00.038
Let's see how you stand up
to pure grain alcohol!

00:13:09.089 --> 00:13:10.632
Hello.

00:13:10.716 --> 00:13:12.175
What's this flaming pool?

00:13:12.259 --> 00:13:14.177
You mean the
company lava pit

00:13:14.261 --> 00:13:16.763
that goes all the way
to the Earth's fiery core?

00:13:16.847 --> 00:13:18.765
Uh, I don't know.

00:13:18.849 --> 00:13:20.142
The core?

00:13:20.225 --> 00:13:22.019
Oh, this is too easy.

00:13:22.102 --> 00:13:25.981
Once I make my way there,
your planet will go micro-nova

00:13:26.064 --> 00:13:30.611
and become a miniature sun,
with me as its Supreme Alderman.

00:13:33.155 --> 00:13:34.948
Oh, no, you probably don't!

00:13:45.208 --> 00:13:47.753
Gotcha.

00:13:49.838 --> 00:13:51.757
If I can't extinguish you,

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:53.759
I'll take you
where there's nothing flammable,

00:13:53.842 --> 00:13:55.844
so you can't do any more harm.

00:14:02.976 --> 00:14:03.977
Turn back, Bender!

00:14:04.061 --> 00:14:05.062
Turn back or else!

00:14:05.145 --> 00:14:07.773
Or else what?

00:14:07.856 --> 00:14:09.608
Oh, or else that.

00:14:13.111 --> 00:14:16.698
Nice try, flame bag, but now
you're trapped here with me

00:14:16.782 --> 00:14:18.575
for the next billion years.

00:14:18.659 --> 00:14:20.702
I've saved the entire world!

00:14:20.786 --> 00:14:23.413
And no one will ever know.

00:14:49.481 --> 00:14:51.149
Uh, yes, hi.

00:14:51.233 --> 00:14:53.777
I'm from the vampire
bank that burned down.

00:14:53.860 --> 00:14:55.696
I have what remains
of the contents

00:14:55.779 --> 00:14:59.616
of a safe deposit box belonging
to a Bender B. Rodriguez.

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:01.285
Ah, thank you.

00:15:03.245 --> 00:15:04.746
Bender's medal.

00:15:04.830 --> 00:15:06.873
It melted in the fire.

00:15:06.957 --> 00:15:09.543
Wait a second.

00:15:13.255 --> 00:15:15.507
You can't
keep me here forever.

00:15:15.591 --> 00:15:18.927
Sooner or later, a polar bear
will happen by.

00:15:19.011 --> 00:15:21.930
A nice, flammable polar bear.

00:15:22.014 --> 00:15:23.724
Polar bears don't burn.

00:15:23.807 --> 00:15:25.642
I've tried many times.

00:15:25.726 --> 00:15:26.727
Huh?

00:15:30.188 --> 00:15:31.189
Bender!

00:15:31.273 --> 00:15:33.025
Fry? How'd you find me?

00:15:33.108 --> 00:15:35.110
I used the
"Find My Robot" app.

00:15:35.193 --> 00:15:38.155
Neat. What was it, 99 cents?

00:15:38.238 --> 00:15:39.907
No, free. But it's got ads on it.

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:41.700
That seems fair.

00:15:41.783 --> 00:15:44.661
Look, Bender, I'm sorry
for doubting you.

00:15:44.745 --> 00:15:47.039
I realize now that
you're a true hero,

00:15:47.122 --> 00:15:49.374
not a glory-seeking arsonist.

00:15:49.458 --> 00:15:50.709
How'd you figure it out?

00:15:50.792 --> 00:15:52.085
Your burnt-up medal.

00:15:52.169 --> 00:15:54.004
I know you would never set a fire

00:15:54.087 --> 00:15:56.882
that would endanger your own valuables.

00:15:56.965 --> 00:15:58.717
Pfft! Of course not.

00:15:58.800 --> 00:16:00.844
It was a psychotic
flame creature from the sun

00:16:00.928 --> 00:16:02.346
who set those fires.

00:16:02.429 --> 00:16:03.847
Flame creature?

00:16:03.931 --> 00:16:06.975
That's right.
Fry, meet Flame-O.

00:16:07.059 --> 00:16:08.393
That's not a flame creature.

00:16:08.477 --> 00:16:10.354
It's your pilot light.

00:16:10.437 --> 00:16:13.065
No. It's a fire monster
from outer space,

00:16:13.148 --> 00:16:16.610
and I'm heroically saving
the world by trapping him here.

00:16:16.693 --> 00:16:19.029
So it was you.

00:16:20.030 --> 00:16:21.448
You're so desperate for glory,

00:16:21.531 --> 00:16:23.742
you made up this whole crazy story.

00:16:23.825 --> 00:16:25.702
Here's your medal, "hero."

00:16:38.465 --> 00:16:40.133
Stupid Bender.

00:16:40.217 --> 00:16:42.803
Liar, liar, pants on fire.

00:16:50.227 --> 00:16:52.688
There, finished.

00:16:52.771 --> 00:16:55.732
Man, I'm good at this, eh, Flame-O?

00:16:56.817 --> 00:16:58.527
Yo, Flame-O.

00:17:11.665 --> 00:17:14.585
So, where's the fire this time?

00:17:14.668 --> 00:17:15.877
- Here.
- Where?

00:17:15.961 --> 00:17:17.087
Here!

00:17:17.170 --> 00:17:19.089
Literally, here!

00:17:39.443 --> 00:17:41.403
It's like the flame
has a mind of its own!

00:17:41.486 --> 00:17:42.529
It's deaky!

00:17:42.613 --> 00:17:43.739
Freaky deaky!

00:17:48.785 --> 00:17:50.537
This fire's unstoppable!

00:17:50.621 --> 00:17:52.164
Thank God
we all got out of there.

00:17:52.247 --> 00:17:53.999
Someone save me!

00:17:55.083 --> 00:17:56.460
I made a rope from my clothes,

00:17:56.543 --> 00:17:58.420
but then this fire started.

00:17:58.503 --> 00:18:00.130
Raise the main ladder!

00:18:04.509 --> 00:18:06.303
Don't lose hope, Fry!

00:18:06.386 --> 00:18:08.430
What kind of coffin do you want?

00:18:17.689 --> 00:18:18.690
Bender?

00:18:18.774 --> 00:18:20.734
I should have known
you started this fire.

00:18:20.817 --> 00:18:22.277
Just another chance
to be a hero.

00:18:22.361 --> 00:18:24.029
Well, you're not saving me.

00:18:24.112 --> 00:18:25.948
Not this time.

00:18:26.031 --> 00:18:27.866
I don't have time
for this shazbot.

00:18:27.950 --> 00:18:30.118
You're getting heroed,
whether you like it or...

00:18:37.793 --> 00:18:41.338
If you're done saving me from
the fire monster from the sun,

00:18:41.421 --> 00:18:43.048
I'll be on my way.

00:18:45.467 --> 00:18:48.262
I guess some grown men
just don't like being carried.

00:18:48.345 --> 00:18:49.930
Thank you, Bender.

00:18:50.013 --> 00:18:52.015
You brought me
right to the lava pit.

00:18:54.142 --> 00:18:55.811
And another thing.

00:18:55.894 --> 00:18:57.479
If someone gives you
a nice medal,

00:18:57.563 --> 00:18:59.898
you should be responsible enough
to care for it.

00:18:59.982 --> 00:19:01.567
- Fry?
- Yeah?

00:19:01.650 --> 00:19:03.694
Shut up!
I got to do hero stuff.

00:19:05.070 --> 00:19:08.532
All the lava in the world
won't wash away your lies.

00:19:16.123 --> 00:19:19.084
We are the Mystic Aldermen of the Sun.

00:19:19.167 --> 00:19:20.294
Okay.

00:19:20.377 --> 00:19:22.087
Stand back, please.

00:19:22.170 --> 00:19:23.964
Okay.

00:19:26.466 --> 00:19:29.094
Unhand me!

00:19:29.177 --> 00:19:31.513
Thank you for your heroism, Earth Robot.

00:19:32.431 --> 00:19:34.141
You have saved
your planet

00:19:34.224 --> 00:19:36.935
from becoming a lifeless ball of fire.

00:19:37.019 --> 00:19:40.480
You are now the greatest hero
in Earth's history.

00:19:40.564 --> 00:19:41.690
Yes!

00:19:41.773 --> 00:19:42.858
Suck it, Gilgamesh!

00:19:42.941 --> 00:19:44.610
Good-bye forever.

00:19:44.693 --> 00:19:47.404
No! I won't go back! I won't!

00:19:49.072 --> 00:19:50.240
Holy crap!

00:19:50.324 --> 00:19:52.409
All your crazy stories were true!

00:19:52.492 --> 00:19:54.494
You saved the entire Earth!

00:19:54.578 --> 00:19:56.455
Yes. Yes, I did.

00:19:57.998 --> 00:19:59.541
But no one will
ever believe me.

00:19:59.625 --> 00:20:01.877
Yes. They will. I'll vouch for you.

00:20:01.960 --> 00:20:04.296
No. They won't believe you either.

00:20:04.379 --> 00:20:05.923
If you even tell anyone I was here,

00:20:06.006 --> 00:20:07.674
they'll say I set the fire.

00:20:07.758 --> 00:20:10.886
So, please, for me, cram it?

00:20:10.969 --> 00:20:12.763
No! The world
has to know that...

00:20:12.846 --> 00:20:15.224
Fry? Are you down here?

00:20:16.600 --> 00:20:18.143
He's all right!

00:20:18.227 --> 00:20:19.978
Praise Gilgamesh!

00:20:25.901 --> 00:20:27.569
So you started the fire?

00:20:27.653 --> 00:20:29.404
I'm afraid so.

00:20:29.488 --> 00:20:31.406
Bender was thousands of miles away.

00:20:31.490 --> 00:20:34.326
I guess a welding torch
is no way to catch a rat.

00:20:35.786 --> 00:20:37.663
This is coming
out of your pay!

00:20:37.746 --> 00:20:39.164
Well, I'm back.

00:20:39.248 --> 00:20:41.875
What'd I miss?
Looks like the building burned down.

00:20:41.959 --> 00:20:44.378
Yeah, thanks to this dope.

00:20:44.461 --> 00:20:46.255
Fry did it?

00:20:46.338 --> 00:20:47.464
Ow!

00:20:47.547 --> 00:20:48.882
You're a horrible person!

00:20:48.966 --> 00:20:52.553
And your carelessness nearly
cost the life of my best friend.

00:20:52.636 --> 00:20:54.054
You.

00:21:00.769 --> 00:21:02.187
Ow!

00:21:02.271 --> 00:21:03.438
Ow!